1
00:01:48,320 --> 00:01:49,160
Hello?

2
00:02:06,400 --> 00:02:07,320
What are you doing here?

3
00:02:07,880 --> 00:02:09,800
You're so busy
you almost forgot your own birthday.

4
00:02:09,880 --> 00:02:11,800
I was afraid I wouldn't catch you
before midnight,

5
00:02:11,880 --> 00:02:12,800
so I came over myself.

6
00:02:13,960 --> 00:02:15,160
I'm sorry.

7
00:02:15,240 --> 00:02:16,920
I've been swamped all day.

8
00:02:17,000 --> 00:02:19,360
I was in the lab all day without my phone.

9
00:02:20,440 --> 00:02:22,000
We still have time. Get in the car.

10
00:02:53,320 --> 00:02:55,920
Happy birthday, Zheng Yu.

11
00:03:08,760 --> 00:03:09,960
Make a wish.

12
00:03:13,160 --> 00:03:16,280
What's wrong? Don't you have
any wishes you want to fulfill?

13
00:03:18,920 --> 00:03:20,400
That's not it.

14
00:03:20,920 --> 00:03:24,400
It's just that I feel like I can achieve
the things I want to do myself.

15
00:03:24,480 --> 00:03:27,040
Rather than making a wish,

16
00:03:27,120 --> 00:03:28,600
I'd rather believe in myself.

17
00:03:32,760 --> 00:03:33,960
Still,

18
00:03:34,040 --> 00:03:36,600
candles are meant to be blown out,
and cake is meant to be eaten.

19
00:03:57,480 --> 00:03:58,320
Oh, right.

20
00:04:01,680 --> 00:04:03,440
Here's your gift. Open it.

21
00:04:13,000 --> 00:04:14,040
A camera?

22
00:04:16,200 --> 00:04:19,839
When we had dinner with Eleonore,
I noticed you really liked her camera.

23
00:04:21,079 --> 00:04:22,480
Thank you. I like it so much.

24
00:04:25,320 --> 00:04:26,760
Now we can use it

25
00:04:26,840 --> 00:04:29,360
to capture more moments together.

26
00:04:31,920 --> 00:04:34,160
I… I wasn't ready.

27
00:04:35,160 --> 00:04:36,920
I think it looks great. Look.

28
00:04:37,000 --> 00:04:38,520
What's so great about it?

29
00:04:38,600 --> 00:04:40,080
My eyes are closed.

30
00:04:41,720 --> 00:04:43,160
That's called being natural.

31
00:04:43,240 --> 00:04:45,240
Look at the photos you usually take.

32
00:04:45,320 --> 00:04:47,840
Every single one
is as stiff as an ID photo.

33
00:04:49,000 --> 00:04:50,200
No, they aren't.

34
00:04:51,520 --> 00:04:52,760
I'll find one and show you.

35
00:04:53,600 --> 00:04:54,760
What are you doing?

36
00:04:56,200 --> 00:04:57,080
This one's pretty good.

37
00:04:57,160 --> 00:05:00,440
What's good about it?
My mouth is wide open!

38
00:05:00,520 --> 00:05:02,840
That's called being natural.
Look at your usual photos.

39
00:05:02,920 --> 00:05:05,280
- You're always so stiff, just like--
- Don't you dare.

40
00:05:12,960 --> 00:05:14,240
Give it to me.

41
00:05:14,320 --> 00:05:15,600
I think this photo is pretty good.

42
00:05:15,680 --> 00:05:18,040
- Give it to me! You made me look bad!
- I'll help you take one more.

43
00:05:18,120 --> 00:05:19,200
- Let me do it!
- One more!

44
00:05:19,280 --> 00:05:21,320
- Give it back!
- One last shot! I'll take a proper one.

45
00:05:21,400 --> 00:05:23,040
- Give it to me!
- One last chance!

46
00:05:34,840 --> 00:05:35,720
What's wrong?

47
00:05:37,240 --> 00:05:38,400
I have a question.

48
00:05:39,800 --> 00:05:40,640
Go ahead.

49
00:05:42,320 --> 00:05:45,160
You spend all day doing lab work.

50
00:05:45,240 --> 00:05:46,560
How do you still have abs?

51
00:05:52,520 --> 00:05:53,480
That's your question?

52
00:05:59,080 --> 00:06:03,200
When doing lab work, to a certain extent,
frequent standing and manual procedures

53
00:06:03,280 --> 00:06:06,240
keep your core muscles
in a state of static activation.

54
00:06:08,360 --> 00:06:11,520
Are you really calling doing lab work

55
00:06:11,600 --> 00:06:12,520
a workout?

56
00:06:13,760 --> 00:06:15,400
I do other exercises too.

57
00:06:15,480 --> 00:06:19,000
After all, research work eventually
comes down to physical endurance too.

58
00:06:19,880 --> 00:06:21,560
Does that answer satisfy you, Ms. Zheng?

59
00:06:25,120 --> 00:06:26,000
Well…

60
00:06:27,000 --> 00:06:27,920
Can I touch them?

61
00:06:31,720 --> 00:06:33,640
Consider it my birthday perk.

62
00:06:35,160 --> 00:06:36,000
Sure.

63
00:06:42,920 --> 00:06:44,520
Just to be clear,

64
00:06:44,600 --> 00:06:47,800
I'm purely curious.

65
00:06:48,440 --> 00:06:50,040
My intentions are completely innocent.

66
00:06:57,040 --> 00:06:58,160
Well, mine aren't.

67
00:07:33,600 --> 00:07:34,520
Zheng Yu…

68
00:08:30,320 --> 00:08:32,320
Why did it suddenly get so cold?

69
00:08:32,400 --> 00:08:34,320
Make sure to dress warmly
when you go to the lab today.

70
00:08:36,400 --> 00:08:39,240
Who told you to lie to Xiaomian last time
about it suddenly getting colder?

71
00:08:39,320 --> 00:08:41,840
Look at it now.
His words actually came true.

72
00:08:42,919 --> 00:08:45,560
Wait, are you still holding a grudge?

73
00:08:46,920 --> 00:08:48,960
You kept our relationship a secret.
Of course I am.

74
00:08:50,000 --> 00:08:52,160
Didn't I already make up for it?

75
00:08:54,320 --> 00:08:55,160
Eat up.

76
00:09:07,680 --> 00:09:09,960
<i>I knew you were acting suspicious lately!</i>

77
00:09:10,040 --> 00:09:12,600
<i>Did I pull so many all-nighters</i>
<i>in the lab that I'm hallucinating?</i>

78
00:09:12,680 --> 00:09:14,720
<i>This has to be</i>
<i>an overseas scam targeting me.</i>

79
00:09:14,800 --> 00:09:16,800
<i>Congratulations!</i>

80
00:09:16,880 --> 00:09:19,120
<i>So this is the new roommate</i>
<i>who is a really good person?</i>

81
00:09:19,200 --> 00:09:20,640
<i>He looks pretty familiar.</i>

82
00:09:20,720 --> 00:09:22,360
<i>I see right through it,</i>
<i>but I'm staying quiet.</i>

83
00:09:22,440 --> 00:09:24,560
<i>You're already a college student,</i>
<i>can't you read the room?</i>

84
00:09:24,640 --> 00:09:27,040
<i>Ms. Zheng, I love you!</i>

85
00:09:27,120 --> 00:09:28,080
<i>Congratulations!</i>

86
00:09:28,160 --> 00:09:29,960
<i>Are my eyes playing tricks on me?</i>

87
00:09:30,520 --> 00:09:32,920
<i>I just put on my new prescription glasses.</i>

88
00:09:33,000 --> 00:09:34,840
<i>I don't think your eyes</i>
<i>are playing tricks on you.</i>

89
00:09:34,920 --> 00:09:37,760
<i>Why am I so shy to click on this?</i>

90
00:09:39,000 --> 00:09:41,120
I told my parents last night
about us being together.

91
00:09:43,640 --> 00:09:45,160
You… What did you say?

92
00:09:46,440 --> 00:09:48,280
You already posted on Moments, didn't you?

93
00:09:48,360 --> 00:09:50,360
So it's only natural that I tell them.

94
00:09:52,040 --> 00:09:53,560
What did your parents say?

95
00:09:54,960 --> 00:09:56,320
They didn't say much.

96
00:10:00,480 --> 00:10:02,280
They just complained that
I moved way too slowly.

97
00:10:02,360 --> 00:10:05,960
They said if I'd been a bit more proactive
back when you were still in Qingyi,

98
00:10:06,040 --> 00:10:08,680
they could have found an excuse
to invite you over for dinner.

99
00:10:10,760 --> 00:10:11,600
They also said

100
00:10:11,680 --> 00:10:14,280
I should share your WeChat with them
so you can chat sometime.

101
00:10:15,800 --> 00:10:17,800
Okay. Go ahead and share it.

102
00:10:19,080 --> 00:10:20,240
Wait, no.

103
00:10:21,120 --> 00:10:23,200
Shouldn't I reach out to them first?

104
00:10:23,840 --> 00:10:26,520
Why don't you share their contacts
with me? I'll add them myself.

105
00:10:26,600 --> 00:10:29,640
I'll arrange a time with them
for a video call.

106
00:10:31,400 --> 00:10:32,600
Really?

107
00:10:41,160 --> 00:10:44,320
Since that's settled, and they're
calling now, why don't we just--

108
00:10:44,400 --> 00:10:45,720
Wait!

109
00:10:47,240 --> 00:10:48,600
I'm not ready!

110
00:10:57,600 --> 00:10:58,880
ALARM

111
00:10:59,600 --> 00:11:01,920
Chen Yanzhou! How dare you trick me!

112
00:11:02,520 --> 00:11:04,840
- I'll teach you a lesson!
- Hey, friendly reminder!

113
00:11:04,920 --> 00:11:07,200
If you don't get changed now,
you'll be late for class.

114
00:11:08,960 --> 00:11:10,680
Well, you'll be late for your work too!

115
00:11:12,080 --> 00:11:13,960
Do we really have to
destroy each other like this?

116
00:11:16,920 --> 00:11:20,440
I'll settle the score
with you after class then.

117
00:11:28,480 --> 00:11:29,960
I'll get going.

118
00:11:31,440 --> 00:11:32,400
Be safe.

119
00:11:33,600 --> 00:11:34,480
Bye.

120
00:12:35,800 --> 00:12:36,960
I'm back.

121
00:13:27,320 --> 00:13:29,280
I wonder if there's a paper titled,

122
00:13:29,360 --> 00:13:31,800
"How to Deal With a Girlfriend
Who's Too Into Studying."

123
00:13:31,880 --> 00:13:33,240
There probably is.

124
00:13:35,040 --> 00:13:36,320
Or maybe,

125
00:13:36,400 --> 00:13:40,480
"On the Dangers of Having a Girlfriend
Who Only Cares About Studying,

126
00:13:40,560 --> 00:13:41,720
and How to Deal With Them."

127
00:13:50,840 --> 00:13:53,760
Who was it this morning who said she'd
settle the score with me after class?

128
00:13:54,920 --> 00:13:56,160
And now that I'm back,

129
00:13:56,240 --> 00:13:59,360
forget settling scores,
you're completely ignoring me.

130
00:14:00,920 --> 00:14:03,080
Who begs someone
to settle a score with them?

131
00:14:07,680 --> 00:14:09,840
The project timeline has been moved up.

132
00:14:11,320 --> 00:14:12,200
Moved up?

133
00:14:14,160 --> 00:14:16,080
My advisor sent an email about it.

134
00:14:16,160 --> 00:14:19,160
So from now on, I might be really busy
and won't have much time for you.

135
00:14:41,720 --> 00:14:43,040
What are you doing?

136
00:14:43,640 --> 00:14:45,080
Who says you won't have time for me?

137
00:14:45,880 --> 00:14:47,560
You can keep me company while I study.

138
00:17:45,320 --> 00:17:46,280
Why are you rushing over?

139
00:17:47,600 --> 00:17:50,320
Don't tell me you knew I'd be working late

140
00:17:51,480 --> 00:17:53,000
and came all the way here to pick me up.

141
00:17:54,120 --> 00:17:57,240
I just got off work,
and I thought I might catch you here.

142
00:17:58,520 --> 00:17:59,920
I was worried earlier

143
00:18:00,000 --> 00:18:02,480
that I'd be too busy
to spend time with you.

144
00:18:03,120 --> 00:18:04,920
Looks like I was overthinking it.

145
00:18:05,920 --> 00:18:08,160
You seem to be even busier than I am.

146
00:18:13,680 --> 00:18:14,520
What's wrong?

147
00:18:17,880 --> 00:18:20,960
I had a meeting with my professor today
and got totally chewed out.

148
00:18:21,040 --> 00:18:24,680
Our whole previous training plan
has to be completely scrapped.

149
00:18:25,200 --> 00:18:26,680
We might have to start over from scratch.

150
00:18:26,760 --> 00:18:28,960
Then what about
your presentation next week?

151
00:18:29,680 --> 00:18:32,680
Marco said we should just
tell them the truth.

152
00:18:32,760 --> 00:18:35,520
They're more interested in
how we work through the problems.

153
00:18:36,720 --> 00:18:37,560
But I…

154
00:18:37,640 --> 00:18:40,600
But you still want
to deliver solid results.

155
00:18:45,440 --> 00:18:46,280
Chen Yanzhou.

156
00:18:46,360 --> 00:18:49,840
Do you remember
when you took a leave of absence?

157
00:18:49,920 --> 00:18:51,240
You took a whole year off,

158
00:18:51,320 --> 00:18:53,440
yet you still won the Vitality Award
when you came back.

159
00:18:53,520 --> 00:18:54,680
And for this internship,

160
00:18:54,760 --> 00:18:58,000
so many people applied,
but in the end,

161
00:18:58,080 --> 00:19:01,200
you were the one who passed the interview
and got the spot.

162
00:19:01,280 --> 00:19:02,480
This time will be the same.

163
00:19:04,680 --> 00:19:05,960
This time is different.

164
00:19:07,320 --> 00:19:08,440
How is it different?

165
00:19:11,160 --> 00:19:12,320
This time,

166
00:19:13,080 --> 00:19:14,400
I'm not alone.

167
00:19:16,880 --> 00:19:18,160
That's true.

168
00:19:21,640 --> 00:19:23,720
So how are things on your end?

169
00:19:23,800 --> 00:19:25,760
I still have a lot to revise.

170
00:19:26,800 --> 00:19:28,840
The professor will be back
from his business trip soon.

171
00:19:28,920 --> 00:19:30,920
Part of me is dreading his return,

172
00:19:31,000 --> 00:19:34,160
but I also hope he comes back soon
so we can work more efficiently.

173
00:19:37,040 --> 00:19:39,200
We really are partners in misery,
aren't we?

174
00:19:40,720 --> 00:19:42,400
Who's your partner
in misery?

175
00:19:43,840 --> 00:19:45,480
Then what do you think
we are right now?

176
00:19:47,040 --> 00:19:48,520
We're

177
00:19:48,600 --> 00:19:51,160
two poor souls
in a foreign land

178
00:19:51,240 --> 00:19:54,800
getting tortured
by experiments.

179
00:19:56,280 --> 00:19:57,520
In that case,

180
00:19:57,600 --> 00:19:59,240
we might as well
comfort each other.

181
00:20:14,720 --> 00:20:16,200
Come on. Let's go home.

182
00:21:35,480 --> 00:21:36,640
What brings you here?

183
00:21:37,360 --> 00:21:39,280
You've been at it for so long.
You need to take a break.

184
00:21:40,480 --> 00:21:42,400
All right. Let's go eat.

185
00:21:42,960 --> 00:21:44,240
Actually,

186
00:21:45,160 --> 00:21:46,760
I brought you a gift.

187
00:21:49,080 --> 00:21:50,320
What is it?

188
00:21:52,440 --> 00:21:54,200
Is the professor who yelled
at you around today?

189
00:21:54,280 --> 00:21:55,600
Where's his office?

190
00:21:55,680 --> 00:21:56,880
I'll smash his windows.

191
00:22:00,720 --> 00:22:02,840
If the institute kicks me out,

192
00:22:02,920 --> 00:22:04,960
I'll have no choice
but to stay home and cook for you.

193
00:22:05,040 --> 00:22:06,600
You'll definitely get tired of me then.

194
00:22:08,840 --> 00:22:10,160
You finally smiled.

195
00:22:14,680 --> 00:22:16,000
Don't worry about me.

196
00:22:17,200 --> 00:22:19,280
Rest assured, I'll never get tired of you.

197
00:22:20,440 --> 00:22:21,280
Really?

198
00:22:22,320 --> 00:22:23,520
Even if the project starts over,

199
00:22:23,600 --> 00:22:26,600
or if you get kicked out of the lab
and have to stay at home,

200
00:22:26,680 --> 00:22:27,760
I won't ever get tired of you.

201
00:22:41,440 --> 00:22:43,440
Come on. Let's get something to eat.

202
00:22:46,560 --> 00:22:47,680
What do you feel like eating?

203
00:22:48,600 --> 00:22:52,280
Is there anything that'll give me the
strength to face the professor's judgment?

204
00:22:53,200 --> 00:22:54,040
Sichuan food?

205
00:22:54,840 --> 00:22:55,840
Hot pot?

206
00:22:56,400 --> 00:22:57,600
Or…

207
00:22:59,120 --> 00:23:00,800
I could pick up a stone for you too.

208
00:23:00,880 --> 00:23:02,000
No way!

209
00:23:02,080 --> 00:23:05,160
- There's a big one over there!
- No, I don't want to get expelled!

210
00:23:13,640 --> 00:23:14,640
<i>My class is over.</i>

211
00:23:14,720 --> 00:23:15,640
CHEN YANZHOU

212
00:23:15,720 --> 00:23:18,000
<i>And I'm about to give my presentation.</i>

213
00:23:20,200 --> 00:23:21,160
<i>Good luck.</i>

214
00:23:21,240 --> 00:23:22,280
<i>You got this!</i>

215
00:24:29,760 --> 00:24:31,800
<i>Today's progress presentation is over.</i>

216
00:24:31,880 --> 00:24:33,480
<i>Marco said we should</i>
<i>go out for a big meal.</i>

217
00:24:33,560 --> 00:24:34,680
<i>I'm joining them,</i>

218
00:24:34,760 --> 00:24:35,840
<i>so I'll be home</i>
<i>a little late.</i>

219
00:24:36,720 --> 00:24:37,640
<i>Okay.</i>

220
00:25:56,200 --> 00:25:58,840
Didn't you say you were going to a party?

221
00:26:00,520 --> 00:26:01,680
They rescheduled.

222
00:26:02,520 --> 00:26:04,400
Tomorrow,
I'll still come pick you up here.

223
00:26:06,120 --> 00:26:08,360
You don't have to. You're busy too.

224
00:26:09,440 --> 00:26:11,280
No matter how busy I am,
I still get off work.

225
00:26:12,760 --> 00:26:16,040
It's only a 15-minute walk
from the subway station to home.

226
00:26:16,120 --> 00:26:18,720
For those 15 minutes,
we don't have to think about anything.

227
00:26:19,760 --> 00:26:20,960
Nothing at all?

228
00:26:25,000 --> 00:26:26,280
No experiments,

229
00:26:26,360 --> 00:26:27,880
no papers,

230
00:26:27,960 --> 00:26:29,880
and no thinking about
what the professor said.

231
00:26:30,560 --> 00:26:31,720
Just look at the trees

232
00:26:32,480 --> 00:26:34,000
or the stars in the sky.

233
00:26:34,960 --> 00:26:36,080
Or

234
00:26:36,160 --> 00:26:37,320
you can just look at me.

235
00:26:38,400 --> 00:26:39,760
What's there to look at?

236
00:26:41,040 --> 00:26:43,040
- Am I not good-looking?
- Narcissist.

237
00:26:44,520 --> 00:26:45,520
Chen Yanzhou.

238
00:26:49,120 --> 00:26:50,000
Thank you.

239
00:26:51,040 --> 00:26:51,880
For what?

240
00:26:53,200 --> 00:26:54,560
For coming to pick me up.

241
00:26:56,640 --> 00:26:57,520
Feeling better?

242
00:26:58,600 --> 00:26:59,640
I'm still upset.

243
00:27:00,240 --> 00:27:03,440
But once I get through this,
I still have to do what needs to be done.

244
00:27:08,880 --> 00:27:11,360
Then just keep going.
Don't be afraid of the outcome.

245
00:27:12,040 --> 00:27:13,120
Either way,

246
00:27:14,320 --> 00:27:15,960
I'll still be here
to pick you up tomorrow.

247
00:27:20,040 --> 00:27:21,240
Let's go.

248
00:28:06,640 --> 00:28:07,520
Zheng Yu.

249
00:28:14,920 --> 00:28:16,080
Are you cold?

250
00:28:17,960 --> 00:28:18,960
Let's go.

251
00:28:58,000 --> 00:28:59,920
What are you doing?

252
00:29:01,920 --> 00:29:02,800
Taking a break.

253
00:29:25,560 --> 00:29:26,680
What are you doing?

254
00:29:29,040 --> 00:29:30,000
Taking a break with you.

255
00:30:08,400 --> 00:30:09,800
Tell me.

256
00:30:09,880 --> 00:30:11,960
Why is it that even when we're exhausted,

257
00:30:12,920 --> 00:30:14,320
we still can't fall asleep?

258
00:30:15,000 --> 00:30:17,760
It's because the brain
is in a state of hyperarousal.

259
00:30:18,640 --> 00:30:20,440
Even when the body is exhausted,

260
00:30:20,520 --> 00:30:22,800
the sympathetic
nervous system stays active.

261
00:30:25,320 --> 00:30:26,560
Are you feeling anxious?

262
00:30:33,480 --> 00:30:34,320
Zheng Yu.

263
00:30:35,600 --> 00:30:37,080
It's okay to fail in life.

264
00:30:39,600 --> 00:30:41,760
I used to have a hard time accepting that,

265
00:30:41,840 --> 00:30:45,040
so I pushed myself
until I had to take a leave of absence.

266
00:30:46,000 --> 00:30:47,320
But even then,

267
00:30:48,120 --> 00:30:49,720
the world didn't come crashing down.

268
00:30:51,120 --> 00:30:53,400
Your professor let you join
the project team

269
00:30:53,480 --> 00:30:55,600
because of how well you wrote
that previous paper, right?

270
00:30:59,360 --> 00:31:02,120
So this is a reward, not a burden.

271
00:31:03,160 --> 00:31:04,080
A reward?

272
00:31:06,200 --> 00:31:08,000
A reward for all your hard work before.

273
00:31:08,080 --> 00:31:10,400
Even if you can't continue with it,

274
00:31:10,480 --> 00:31:13,320
you'll just go back to being
a student like everyone else.

275
00:31:14,000 --> 00:31:15,800
You'll go to class, do your assignments,

276
00:31:15,880 --> 00:31:19,000
or apply to join
another professor's project team.

277
00:31:20,320 --> 00:31:22,960
You haven't fallen off a cliff.

278
00:31:23,040 --> 00:31:24,840
You've just returned to solid ground.

279
00:31:34,400 --> 00:31:35,600
You're right.

280
00:31:36,240 --> 00:31:37,920
I need to loosen up a bit.

281
00:31:46,600 --> 00:31:49,400
I suddenly really want to go
to the beach and watch the sunrise.

282
00:31:53,400 --> 00:31:55,760
Why don't we find
some time to go later on?

283
00:31:58,760 --> 00:32:00,200
We don't need to find time later.

284
00:32:02,320 --> 00:32:03,680
We can go right now.

285
00:32:04,960 --> 00:32:05,920
Right now?

286
00:32:08,120 --> 00:32:09,720
We can't sleep anyway,

287
00:32:09,800 --> 00:32:11,200
so instead of lying here wide awake,

288
00:32:11,280 --> 00:32:13,520
we might as well head to the beach now
and wait for the sunrise.

289
00:32:14,640 --> 00:32:16,160
If we leave right now,

290
00:32:16,240 --> 00:32:18,040
we'll get to the beach just in time.

291
00:32:18,120 --> 00:32:19,120
Really?

292
00:32:19,840 --> 00:32:20,960
Let's go.

293
00:32:21,480 --> 00:32:23,320
Then I'd better get ready!

294
00:32:23,400 --> 00:32:25,920
Should we bring the camera?

295
00:32:26,000 --> 00:32:27,560
And what about the picnic mat?

296
00:32:27,640 --> 00:32:28,680
Where did we put it?

297
00:32:29,360 --> 00:32:31,840
Under the left cabinet
in the storage room, second drawer down.

298
00:32:39,840 --> 00:32:42,920
Do you remember
the last time we saw the sea together?

299
00:32:43,920 --> 00:32:44,800
Qingshan Island.

300
00:32:47,080 --> 00:32:50,160
Come to think of it,
that legend you told me back then

301
00:32:50,240 --> 00:32:51,480
was pretty accurate.

302
00:32:53,200 --> 00:32:55,760
When two people climb up here together,

303
00:32:55,840 --> 00:32:59,800
the direction of travel of the first ship
they see between the lighthouses

304
00:33:00,560 --> 00:33:04,320
is where the two will travel to together
in the future.

305
00:33:05,600 --> 00:33:07,560
Thinking back,
that legend really came true.

306
00:33:08,920 --> 00:33:10,200
Once we graduate and go home,

307
00:33:10,280 --> 00:33:12,560
we should send the Tourism Bureau
a commendation letter.

308
00:33:19,080 --> 00:33:20,360
What are you thinking about?

309
00:33:22,160 --> 00:33:23,880
I was thinking,

310
00:33:23,960 --> 00:33:26,360
maybe I've been
too cautious all this time.

311
00:33:26,880 --> 00:33:31,080
I always thought falling for someone meant
giving yourself another weakness.

312
00:33:31,880 --> 00:33:33,160
But now…

313
00:33:34,520 --> 00:33:35,680
How should I put it?

314
00:33:35,760 --> 00:33:40,360
It's like my heart feels more grounded,
and I've grown stronger.

315
00:33:42,360 --> 00:33:45,240
Carrying things together
is so much lighter

316
00:33:45,920 --> 00:33:47,440
than toughing it out alone.

317
00:33:49,600 --> 00:33:52,840
So from now on, the good and the bad,
I'll share everything with you.

318
00:33:53,920 --> 00:33:54,800
Me too.

319
00:33:56,160 --> 00:33:57,760
Don't keep it all to yourself.

320
00:33:58,280 --> 00:33:59,320
You neither.

321
00:34:30,600 --> 00:34:33,239
<i>I thought you two would go on a trip</i>
<i>once your project wrapped up,</i>

322
00:34:33,320 --> 00:34:35,400
<i>but then he ended up going on</i>
<i>a business trip instead?</i>

323
00:34:36,960 --> 00:34:39,480
The institute sent him out of town.
He didn't really have a choice.

324
00:34:39,560 --> 00:34:42,840
Besides, doesn't this just prove that
his project is going really smoothly?

325
00:34:42,920 --> 00:34:43,800
Isn't that a good thing?

326
00:34:43,880 --> 00:34:45,880
<i>But you haven't seen each other</i>
<i>in half a month!</i>

327
00:34:45,960 --> 00:34:47,440
<i>How can you stay so composed?</i>

328
00:34:48,760 --> 00:34:51,159
I'm not the type of person

329
00:34:51,239 --> 00:34:53,760
who starts crying after being apart
for a few days,

330
00:34:53,840 --> 00:34:56,239
clinging to her phone
and waiting for the other person to reply.

331
00:34:56,320 --> 00:34:58,120
That would be so immature.

332
00:34:59,560 --> 00:35:01,480
<i>Keep denying it.</i>

333
00:35:05,920 --> 00:35:08,720
CHEN YANZHOU, HAVE YOU EATEN?

334
00:35:25,640 --> 00:35:26,960
<i>What took you so long to answer?</i>

335
00:35:28,640 --> 00:35:30,640
I was studying just now
and didn't hear it.

336
00:35:31,680 --> 00:35:33,160
How's the studying going?

337
00:35:34,320 --> 00:35:35,440
Pretty good.

338
00:35:35,520 --> 00:35:37,160
Why is your hair messy?

339
00:35:38,920 --> 00:35:40,080
<i>Not that side.</i>

340
00:35:40,160 --> 00:35:41,600
<i>The hair on your left is sticking up.</i>

341
00:35:43,560 --> 00:35:45,640
No, not there. The bit in front.

342
00:35:50,320 --> 00:35:51,360
I'm not sure that's helping.

343
00:35:56,080 --> 00:35:57,200
It's all your fault.

344
00:35:57,280 --> 00:35:58,800
You were silent all day,

345
00:35:58,880 --> 00:36:01,040
<i>and now you show up bossing me around.</i>

346
00:36:01,120 --> 00:36:02,520
<i>It's not like you can fix it for me.</i>

347
00:36:03,480 --> 00:36:06,080
I was in meetings all day today,
and our phones were collected.

348
00:36:06,160 --> 00:36:07,080
I just got my phone back

349
00:36:07,160 --> 00:36:08,960
<i>and haven't even had time to eat yet.</i>

350
00:36:11,280 --> 00:36:12,720
That sounds so exhausting.

351
00:36:12,800 --> 00:36:14,240
When will it finally be over?

352
00:36:14,320 --> 00:36:15,800
Next week.

353
00:36:15,880 --> 00:36:16,960
It might even end early.

354
00:36:17,560 --> 00:36:18,400
Really?

355
00:36:19,760 --> 00:36:21,800
<i>So just hang in there for a few more days.</i>

356
00:36:21,880 --> 00:36:24,080
After that, no more sitting alone
staring at a phone anymore.

357
00:36:26,000 --> 00:36:28,480
Who's been sitting around
staring at their phone?

358
00:36:31,800 --> 00:36:33,720
I have.

359
00:36:36,200 --> 00:36:38,560
Okay, you should go eat now.

360
00:36:42,440 --> 00:36:44,480
I'm going to hang up then.

361
00:36:45,160 --> 00:36:46,000
Okay.

362
00:36:48,840 --> 00:36:49,760
Bye.

363
00:37:51,720 --> 00:37:52,760
CHEN YANZHOU

364
00:37:52,840 --> 00:37:55,000
<i>The first phase</i>
<i>of the report is finally over.</i>

365
00:37:55,080 --> 00:37:56,560
<i>Walking down the street now,</i>

366
00:37:56,640 --> 00:37:58,080
<i>everything looks so much brighter.</i>

367
00:38:08,760 --> 00:38:10,920
<i>The cherry blossoms in Berlin</i>
<i>are blooming.</i>

368
00:38:23,200 --> 00:38:24,120
XU FANGLI

369
00:38:24,200 --> 00:38:25,720
<i>Since you helped me buy all that stuff,</i>

370
00:38:25,800 --> 00:38:26,840
<i>I'll teach you a trick.</i>

371
00:38:26,920 --> 00:38:28,800
HIGH-LEVEL CUTENESS
AUTHENTIC AND ENDEARING

372
00:38:28,880 --> 00:38:30,960
<i>Next time you video call Chen Yanzhou,</i>

373
00:38:31,040 --> 00:38:35,000
<i>use this trick to revive the spark</i>
<i>that cooled off this past month.</i>

374
00:38:36,680 --> 00:38:37,680
<i>That's silly.</i>

375
00:38:39,120 --> 00:38:43,000
<i>When it comes to relationships,</i>
<i>just missing each other isn't enough.</i>

376
00:38:43,080 --> 00:38:46,160
<i>When you don't see each other for a month,</i>
<i>it's easy to start feeling distant.</i>

377
00:38:46,240 --> 00:38:49,240
<i>The way to bridge the distance</i>
<i>is to express your feelings.</i>

378
00:38:49,320 --> 00:38:52,880
<i>Do you get it?</i>
<i>Just try, you've got nothing to lose.</i>

379
00:38:52,960 --> 00:38:54,760
<i>If it doesn't work,</i>
<i>you can come back and yell at me.</i>

380
00:38:54,840 --> 00:38:56,880
<i>Why aren't you replying?</i>

381
00:38:56,960 --> 00:38:58,280
<i>Don't you trust me?</i>

382
00:38:58,360 --> 00:39:00,480
<i>I do, I do! You're the expert!</i>

383
00:39:18,600 --> 00:39:20,520
<i>Yanzhou, happy birthday.</i>

384
00:39:20,600 --> 00:39:22,720
<i>Are you spending your birthday</i>
<i>with Xiaozheng?</i>

385
00:39:22,800 --> 00:39:25,640
<i>I'm away on a business trip,</i>
<i>and she's in Berlin.</i>

386
00:39:25,720 --> 00:39:26,800
<i>Well, get back to work.</i>

387
00:39:26,880 --> 00:39:28,800
<i>Treat yourself to a nice meal afterward.</i>

388
00:39:53,720 --> 00:39:56,000
No way. Are you completely stunned?

389
00:39:56,760 --> 00:39:58,840
Or did I show up at a bad time?

390
00:40:05,520 --> 00:40:06,640
The cake's getting squashed!

391
00:40:07,440 --> 00:40:08,440
Who cares if it's squashed?

392
00:40:09,440 --> 00:40:10,720
I'm about to get squashed too!

393
00:40:16,040 --> 00:40:16,880
What are you doing?

394
00:40:18,240 --> 00:40:20,920
Didn't you say you were getting squashed?
I'm trying to put you back in shape.

395
00:40:24,240 --> 00:40:27,760
So where are we going to eat the cake?

396
00:40:44,320 --> 00:40:45,440
Was the trip tiring?

397
00:40:45,520 --> 00:40:48,280
Didn't I tell you
I'd be wrapping things up here soon?

398
00:40:48,360 --> 00:40:49,440
Did you forget?

399
00:40:49,520 --> 00:40:51,360
I got your birthday wrong before,

400
00:40:51,440 --> 00:40:53,720
and you said you'd
make me pay for it with interest.

401
00:40:53,800 --> 00:40:56,520
Then we ended up in different countries,
so I couldn't celebrate with you.

402
00:40:56,600 --> 00:41:00,000
I couldn't let your birthday pass again,
or you might really hold a grudge.

403
00:41:00,080 --> 00:41:01,640
So I'm here to pay my debt.

404
00:41:02,840 --> 00:41:04,040
How did you find me?

405
00:41:05,000 --> 00:41:08,880
I saw the hotel photos you posted,
so I thought I'd take a chance.

406
00:41:12,840 --> 00:41:13,960
What's wrong?

407
00:41:14,040 --> 00:41:17,160
If I'd guessed wrong, I'd just think of it
as taking a casual city walk.

408
00:41:17,240 --> 00:41:18,840
If I guessed right…

409
00:41:21,480 --> 00:41:23,840
Happy birthday, Chen Yanzhou.

410
00:41:24,400 --> 00:41:25,600
Make a wish.

411
00:41:27,800 --> 00:41:28,640
You…

412
00:41:28,720 --> 00:41:30,160
I don't need to make a wish.

413
00:41:31,520 --> 00:41:33,000
It's already come true.

414
00:41:35,000 --> 00:41:37,840
So over these past two years,
besides the principal debt,

415
00:41:37,920 --> 00:41:39,440
shouldn't there be interest too?

416
00:41:39,520 --> 00:41:40,360
What is the interest?

417
00:41:45,640 --> 00:41:46,800
Take a guess.

418
00:41:56,480 --> 00:41:57,640
What are you doing?

419
00:41:58,280 --> 00:41:59,600
Collecting the interest.

420
00:42:00,480 --> 00:42:03,720
I was talking about what's inside my bag.
I meant for you to get it yourself.

421
00:42:06,920 --> 00:42:08,880
Looks like I misunderstood then.

422
00:42:10,520 --> 00:42:12,240
You definitely did that on purpose.

423
00:42:16,600 --> 00:42:17,800
A tie?

424
00:42:31,560 --> 00:42:32,720
Why are you smiling?

425
00:42:34,160 --> 00:42:35,000
No reason.

426
00:42:36,440 --> 00:42:37,320
I really like it.

427
00:42:41,360 --> 00:42:43,800
You're putting it on right now?
Why are you in such a rush?

428
00:42:46,040 --> 00:42:46,880
Fair point.

429
00:42:47,600 --> 00:42:50,320
I'll keep it safe for now and wear it
when an important occasion comes up.

430
00:43:10,720 --> 00:43:13,160
I was on a video call
with Ms. Yang a few days ago.

431
00:43:13,240 --> 00:43:14,400
She knew it was your birthday,

432
00:43:14,480 --> 00:43:16,800
so she asked me
to wish you a happy birthday.

433
00:43:16,880 --> 00:43:17,880
You probably haven't heard,

434
00:43:17,960 --> 00:43:20,560
but Ms. Yang moved her mom
to a hospital in another city.

435
00:43:20,640 --> 00:43:23,920
They built a new care center there

436
00:43:24,000 --> 00:43:26,800
specializing in long-term care
for patients in vegetative states.

437
00:43:26,880 --> 00:43:28,920
That should take
a bit of pressure off her as a caregiver.

438
00:43:30,600 --> 00:43:32,680
She's still running
her livestream like before.

439
00:43:33,400 --> 00:43:34,680
It went viral a while back,

440
00:43:34,760 --> 00:43:36,720
so a lot of people started following her,

441
00:43:36,800 --> 00:43:38,480
sending her encouragement and support.

442
00:43:38,560 --> 00:43:41,640
But some people have been nasty too.
I've already reported several accounts.

443
00:43:41,720 --> 00:43:42,560
Oh, right.

444
00:43:42,640 --> 00:43:46,560
Do you remember that convenience store
I used to work part-time at?

445
00:43:46,640 --> 00:43:52,000
My old boss rented two more storefronts
and is hiring managers for them.

446
00:43:52,080 --> 00:43:56,280
A few days ago, he posted that
he wanted to take his son out to play,

447
00:43:56,360 --> 00:43:57,800
and asked for recommendations.

448
00:43:57,880 --> 00:43:59,360
I even left him a comment.

449
00:44:03,320 --> 00:44:06,280
Chen Yanzhou, why are you so quiet?

450
00:44:06,360 --> 00:44:09,320
I just feel like you're like a piggy bank,

451
00:44:09,400 --> 00:44:11,640
clattering and spilling out coins
right in front of me.

452
00:44:11,720 --> 00:44:15,080
Chen Yanzhou! If you think
I talk too much, just say so!

453
00:44:15,160 --> 00:44:16,520
I never said that!

454
00:44:18,600 --> 00:44:21,200
Having you here today
makes me really happy.

455
00:44:22,440 --> 00:44:23,640
Where do you plan to go tomorrow?

456
00:44:24,400 --> 00:44:25,840
I haven't thought about it yet.

457
00:44:28,640 --> 00:44:31,560
- I'll take you out tomorrow afternoon.
- Do you have time?

458
00:44:32,560 --> 00:44:34,160
I've been working overtime
for a whole month.

459
00:44:34,240 --> 00:44:36,120
Taking half a day off
shouldn't be an issue, right?

460
00:44:38,200 --> 00:44:39,320
Let's go.

461
00:44:40,160 --> 00:44:42,120
I just so happen to have
read up on a lot of places.

462
00:44:42,200 --> 00:44:43,720
We can go together.

463
00:44:43,800 --> 00:44:46,280
Charles Bridge is really famous.
We can visit it tomorrow too.

464
00:48:22,920 --> 00:48:27,920
Subtitle translation by: Cempaka Malinja
